# TARGET SAFETY FACTOR q( Psi ) for examples/q-driven.toml -- the INPUT of a
# run in which the toroidal field is an OUTPUT. ROADMAP.md item 10.
#
# THE ABSCISSA IS THE SOURCE'S NORMALISED FLUX, ONE ON THE AXIS, like every
# other profile table in examples/ and unlike meq::FluxSurfaceFamily's own
# label, which is zero there. meq::SafetyFactorSystem owns the reflection
# between them. Handing a table written the other way round does NOT fail: it converges,
# at full order, to an equilibrium with its shear reversed -- which is a real
# configuration a real machine can have, so nothing downstream looks wrong. See
# src/meq/SafetyFactor.hpp section 2.
#
# The three columns are Psi, q and dq/dPsi, which is meq::SplineProfile's
# format: a Hermite cubic needs the slope as well as the value, and MEQ will not
# guess one for you.
#
# WHERE THIS TABLE CAME FROM, so that the example asserts something. It is the
# q of an equilibrium built from the CLOSED FORM g( Psi ) = 2.20 + 0.55 Psi on
# this box AND THIS MESH, measured through q = V' g < R^-2 >/4 pi^2 and
# extracted as every run extracts (psi~ and q~, the continuous pair), AT THE
# LOOP'S OWN KNOTS -- the 19 surfaces rho = j/20 that RefinementLevels = 1 and
# PolynomialDegree = 2 give it -- with three labels between each pair, and at
# the 24 surfaces the run's own surfaces file reports, with three-point
# slopes. Exact at every knot, so the loop reads no interpolation error, and
# exact where the run reports its q, so that comparison reads none either. Same
# mesh and the same extraction on purpose: the discretisation error is then
# common to the measurement and to the loop that inverts it, so what the
# acceptance reads is the LOOP's accuracy and not the mesh's. The loop's
# answer is known independently of the loop: it must recover that g, and
# DriverAcceptance::theDriverSolvesForTheToroidalField asserts it does. A
# target invented rather than measured would only have shown that the loop
# reaches SOME fixed point. QRefiningStudy's writeTheExampleTarget writes it;
# change the mesh or the degree and it is to be written again, since the knots
# follow them.
#
#        Psi                  q                       dq/dPsi
